{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/230631-patchwork-and-the-physical-body","id":230631,"title":"Patchwork and the Physical Body","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-16T16:03:53-07:00","id":230631,"title":"Patchwork and the Physical Body","content":"From the book page 116: &quot;It is possible to build a Cover whole-cloth using the small pieces of other people\u2019s souls acquired through patch jobs.&quot;<br /> <br /> In this case, this new Cover has the same appearance as one of the other Covers the demon has?<br /> Is this new body from one of the pact-makers? If so, what happens to the pact-maker body, is it duplicate for the demon?<br /> As soon as she can buy the first dot of Cover, she can create a whole new body with the appearance she desires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3677-fpmonteiro","name":"fpmonteiro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:52:48-07:00","id":230733,"title":"","content":"This is something where the books fall silent. I assume the demon's player (as opposed to the demon) can design a demons' covers basic appearance, but it will be nondescript and bland in other peoples eyes unless he has threaded in an appropriate contract. So if he wanted the looks to be memorable he would need to have bargained for that. You can look however you want, as long as anything memorable is related to a spliced in contract.<br /> <br /> So if he wanted to have striking green eyes, or an imposing chin, or a stereotypical Jewish nose that people can't help but notice, someone will needed to have sold theirs to him. (At that person would not loose a body part and be blind, chinless or noseless, but would no longer have that feature be distinctive in others people thoughts of him)<br /> <br /> At least until you got the cover to level 5 or more, by then there is so much background the demon could dictate the covers appearance as it wished.<br /> <br /> Related, I also assume that even for the Covers the God Machine creates, anything not Explicitly Specified would be &quot;Proceduraly Generated&quot; by the processes that create the Cover. This is one reason the God Machine cannot just go pick up a newly Fallen Demon at his home or dayjob or wherever. Because they could have been anything that allowed the Angel to accomplish its mission. Heck, the God Machine does not even know the Covers name. There is not really that much minute attention to detail in creating a cover when operating at the God Machines scale.<br /> <br /> A Demon can to it, but it takes effort (getting a patchwork to the level where you get the bonus) For lesser patchworks, the Demon (as opposed to the player) may not even know the Covers name until he coalesces it around himself for the first time, if if is not covered by part of a contract woven into the Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3698-bramble_thorn","name":"Bramble_Thorn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:49:47-07:00","id":233094,"title":"","content":"A patchwork Cover is a mix of the people it's put together from, but doesn't look exactly like any of them. If there's only a single pactee, the demon will look enough like that person to be mistaken for them at a distance, but not enough to fool anyone up close.<br /> <br /> Out of character, I'd let the player design the appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}